      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright © 2015 The Authors. Published by Elsevier Ltd.. All rights reserved.",
        "AbstractText": [
          {
            "NlmCategory": "BACKGROUND",
            "Label": "INTRODUCTION",
            "content": "Spinal hydatid cyst is a rare, but serious condition."
          },
          {
            "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
            "Label": "PRESENTATION OF THE CASE",
            "content": "Herein, we present a 17-year-old male patient with back pain radiating to the legs and progressive weakness in the lower limbs. CT and MRI showed a spinal-paraspinal hydatid cyst with a dumbbell appearance that caused neural foraminal widening and spinal cord compression. The case was explored via right T3-T4 hemilaminectomy, and the hydatid cyst was completely removed."
          },
          {
            "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
            "Label": "DISCUSSION",
            "content": "The clinical presentation, diagnosis, and surgical treatment of this rare case of spinal hydatid disease are discussed, and all published cases of primary dumbbell hydatid cyst are reviewed."
          },
          {
            "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
            "Label": "CONCLUSION",
            "content": "Even if serological test results are negative, hydatid cysts should be considered in the differential diagnosis of cystic lesions of the spine."
          }
        ]
      },
